WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.680
A China-North Korea bridge unused for 12 years opens this week, shifting Northeast Asian trade. This is Omni View, episode 205. The new Yalu River Bridge, completed in 2014, will hold an opening ceremony on Thursday. Chinese state news agency Xinhua presented the event as routine infrastructure progress on Wednesday morning. Vehicles have already been spotted crossing. Traffic signals on the span have been activated. The crossing links the Chinese city of Dandong with North Korea's

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.580
Nuiju. It stretches over the Yalu River on a corridor built for expanded movement once regulatory

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:41.200
and technical requirements were met on both sides. South China Morning Post framed the opening

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.440
as a long-awaited step that could ease logistics between the two countries after years of unexplained

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.860
inaction. In that reading, the idle years were a logistics bottleneck waiting on paperwork,

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:58.200
not a sudden burst of goodwill. South Korean newspaper The Chosun Daily reported that signs of

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.140
an imminent opening appeared last week, including active traffic lights and bridge indicators.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.560
That reporting tied the timing to visible preparations, suggesting both governments had

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:13.500
quietly coordinated the final steps rather than improvising them in public. The finished

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.240
structure had sat idle, even though it occupies a strategic place on a key trade corridor.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.980
The ceremony on Thursday is the next public marker. Vehicles are already using the deck.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:29.268
Russia authorities arrested a journalist from the Japanese newspaper Hokkaido Shimbun,

00:01:29.808 --> 00:01:33.748
accusing him of gathering information on Russian defense capabilities for Tokyo.

00:01:34.528 --> 00:01:40.628
BBC World News reported the charges as part of ongoing tensions between Russia and Japan over security matters.

00:01:41.128 --> 00:01:42.688
The arrest took place in Russia.

00:01:43.268 --> 00:01:47.488
The accusation is that he collected data related to Russian military infrastructure.

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:52.648
Coverage from his own paper emphasized his professional role in reporting regional developments,

00:01:52.648 --> 00:01:54.628
not a covert assignment.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.008
That is the case a newsroom would make.

00:01:57.508 --> 00:02:01.848
A correspondent doing the job the paper sent him to do in a country that has narrowed

00:02:01.848 --> 00:02:03.248
the space for foreign reporters.

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:09.128
BBC World News and the Japanese outlet both placed the incident inside a wider pattern of

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:12.948
restricted access for foreign reporters in Russia since 2022.

00:02:13.688 --> 00:02:18.628
The charges still center on alleged collection of defense information, which Moscow treats

00:02:18.628 --> 00:02:21.328
as espionage even when a byline is attached.

00:02:21.328 --> 00:02:26.228
Supporters of a hard line in Russia would say military infrastructure is not a public

00:02:26.228 --> 00:02:31.088
beat, and that intent is measured by the material gathered, not by the business card.

00:02:31.688 --> 00:02:35.168
Even that argument leaves a limit its own advocates have to live with.

00:02:35.648 --> 00:02:41.228
Once foreign reporting itself is treated as intelligence work, independent accounts of security policy

00:02:41.228 --> 00:02:42.448
become harder to test.

00:02:43.389 --> 00:02:48.909
An electrical storm brought unusual spring hail and flooding to Santiago on Tuesday, damaging

00:02:48.909 --> 00:02:49.989
homes and businesses.

00:02:49.989 --> 00:02:50.169
purposes.

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:55.189
Mirko Press described the event as part of a sequence of weather disruptions, noting

00:02:55.189 --> 00:02:58.669
it came five days after a mudslide in the Las Condas District.

00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:05.049
The Chilean meteorological directorate classified a tornado that formed as EF-0, the weakest

00:03:05.049 --> 00:03:06.269
category on the scale.

00:03:06.709 --> 00:03:11.149
That preliminary rating came from damage assessments, not from a higher end track.

00:03:11.789 --> 00:03:14.649
Authorities issued a red alert for the metropolitan region.

00:03:15.149 --> 00:03:19.769
The National Disaster Prevention and Response Service declared the same red alert across the

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:23.469
capital region and coordinated the response through affected neighborhoods.

00:03:24.089 --> 00:03:27.009
Hale flooded streets, homes, and businesses in the capital.

00:03:27.529 --> 00:03:32.749
The disaster service is the agency now running the alert, five days after the earlier mudslide

00:03:32.749 --> 00:03:33.649
in Las Condas.

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:40.167
Philippine Defense Secretary Gilberto Teodoro, Jr., stated that military-to-military channels

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:41.707
with China will remain closed.

00:03:42.227 --> 00:03:47.747
The Department of National Defense announcement, carried on PTV, framed the suspension as a response

00:03:47.747 --> 00:03:50.807
bonds to ongoing maritime friction in the South China Sea.

00:03:51.287 --> 00:03:55.947
Everything turns on whether that friction and recent public comments from the Chinese embassy

00:03:55.947 --> 00:03:59.547
are reasons to keep those channels shut rather than to reopen them.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:05.027
Teodoro also questioned the embassy's recent criticism, treating the public statements as

00:04:05.027 --> 00:04:07.827
inconsistent with the need for direct military dialogue.

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:13.807
The KC is making is that you cannot scold in public and then demand a private military hotline

00:04:13.807 --> 00:04:16.087
as if the two postures fit together.

00:04:16.087 --> 00:04:16.187
failure.

00:04:16.707 --> 00:04:20.727
Philippine officials have held that position since earlier incidents in the region this

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:20.987
year.

00:04:21.507 --> 00:04:26.347
The suspension prevents routine military contacts between the two nations, including the

00:04:26.347 --> 00:04:28.967
ordinary calls that would otherwise move on a schedule.

00:04:29.587 --> 00:04:34.847
The embassy's criticism is the other half of the argument, as Manila tells it, a public complaint

00:04:34.847 --> 00:04:39.467
that in Teodoro's view does not match a request for closed-door military talk.

00:04:40.027 --> 00:04:44.167
What the briefing does not give is the embassy's own full case in its own words.

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:50.387
only Manila's reply to it. Aviation Analytics firm Sirium forecast that the commercial aircraft

00:04:50.387 --> 00:04:55.887
corporation of China, or KOMAC, will hold 5% of the world's passenger fleet allocation

00:04:55.887 --> 00:05:02.187
by 2045. South China Morning Post presented that projection as evidence of growing Chinese

00:05:02.187 --> 00:05:09.807
manufacturing capacity in civil aviation. Airbus is projected at 47% and Boeing at 39% under

00:05:09.807 --> 00:05:15.807
the same outlook. The forecast assumes continued domestic orders for KOMAC's C919 narrow

00:05:15.807 --> 00:05:23.187
body. Serium's figures put Embraer at 3% and ATR at 2%. Strong order books inside China

00:05:23.187 --> 00:05:28.027
sit alongside global demand for single- Isle aircraft, which is the slice of the market

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:33.947
the C919 is built to enter. The numbers place China's chief civilian aircraft builder behind

00:05:33.947 --> 00:05:39.487
the two established Western manufacturers and ahead of Embraer and ATR in that long-term allocation.

00:05:40.519 --> 00:05:45.979
Singapore's economy grew 5.4% in the July to September quarter, compared with the same

00:05:45.979 --> 00:05:49.599
period a year earlier, according to advanced government estimates.

00:05:50.319 --> 00:05:54.759
Al Jazeera reported the figure as stronger than recent quarters and noted the city state's

00:05:54.759 --> 00:05:57.899
role in regional electronics and data center supply chains.

00:05:58.599 --> 00:06:03.979
Officials linked part of the expansion to demand tied to artificial intelligence or AI infrastructure.

00:06:03.979 --> 00:06:09.659
government statisticians described the growth as broad-based across manufacturing and services.

00:06:10.279 --> 00:06:14.739
Sales of fast tech and AI-related equipment contributed to the measured expansion.

00:06:15.339 --> 00:06:19.119
The result comes amid wider Asian export gains reported this week.

00:06:20.127 --> 00:06:25.267
Hamburg opened a trial, progress worth knowing, against a Ukrainian man accused of leading the group

00:06:25.267 --> 00:06:30.047
that carried out the September 2022 explosions on the Nord Stream gas pipelines.

00:06:30.907 --> 00:06:36.067
Deutschewelle reported that the defendant identified only as Sir He K, under German privacy

00:06:36.067 --> 00:06:38.967
rules, was extradited from Italy last year.

00:06:39.947 --> 00:06:44.567
Investigators say he coordinated professional divers and explosives expert and a boat skipper.

00:06:45.227 --> 00:06:49.947
That group, prosecutors say, plotted to travel to a remote section of the pipelines off the

00:06:49.947 --> 00:06:51.427
Danish coast and blow them up.

00:06:52.127 --> 00:06:57.227
German prosecutors described the operation as a coordinated strike on civilian energy infrastructure.

00:06:57.227 --> 00:07:01.487
The pipelines had carried Russian natural gas to Europe before the attack.

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:06.667
The explosions ruptured Nord Stream 1, which Moscow had switched off a month earlier,

00:07:07.207 --> 00:07:10.687
and destroyed Nord Stream 2, which had yet to come into operation.

00:07:11.327 --> 00:07:16.127
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has denied any official involvement by Kiev.

00:07:16.847 --> 00:07:21.187
The trial opens while European governments continue to adjust energy import patterns

00:07:21.187 --> 00:07:22.587
away from Russian supplies.

00:07:22.587 --> 00:07:27.712
To really understand how a crossing between rival states finally carries traffic,

00:07:28.152 --> 00:07:33.012
you have to look past the ceremony and at the parallel paperwork both sides must finish in private.

00:07:33.572 --> 00:07:38.052
Most coverage treats a sudden activation as simple diplomacy or a burst of goodwill.

00:07:38.652 --> 00:07:45.332
In practice, these projects move only after both sides complete technical and customs arrangements that are rarely announced together.

00:07:45.952 --> 00:07:50.692
That usually means synchronized changes to inspection protocols, currency settlement rules,

00:07:50.692 --> 00:07:53.712
and rail gauge compatibility on each bank of the border.

00:07:54.292 --> 00:07:57.952
Those steps can take years even when political will already exists.

00:07:58.572 --> 00:08:02.932
The friendship bridge between North and South Korea stayed unused for decades until rail

00:08:02.932 --> 00:08:05.352
and customs rules aligned in 2007.

00:08:06.032 --> 00:08:11.712
That is the same pattern, steel in place, traffic still forbidden, until the operating rules match.

00:08:12.352 --> 00:08:16.652
When you hear that a single political meeting unlocked a crossing, the check is whether

00:08:16.652 --> 00:08:21.512
customs or transport ministries on both sides have published updated operating procedures.

00:08:22.564 --> 00:08:25.024
Ceremony coverage will not show you those constraints.

00:08:25.784 --> 00:08:28.004
Primary records from the ministries often will.

00:08:28.664 --> 00:08:33.144
Cross-check official statements against the actual operating documents released by transport

00:08:33.144 --> 00:08:36.304
and customs agencies, not against the speeches alone.

00:08:36.944 --> 00:08:41.764
The document worth looking for is a posted set of updated procedures from both ministries,

00:08:41.764 --> 00:08:46.804
because that is what lets inspectors, banks, and rail operators work to the same clock.

00:08:47.484 --> 00:08:53.164
South China Morning Post frames the Yalu opening as delayed logistics finally moving after unexplained

00:08:53.164 --> 00:08:59.184
inaction, while BBC World News is covering northeast Asian security this week, through the journalist

00:08:59.184 --> 00:09:05.284
arrest in Russia rather than through that infrastructure story. A joint operating manual and tariff schedule

00:09:05.284 --> 00:09:10.984
still have to be posted before commercial traffic can begin in volume. That wraps up today's omniview.

00:09:10.984 --> 00:09:16.084
Remember, the best informed people read more than one perspective, and the calmest ones

00:09:16.084 --> 00:09:19.524
know that most days, somewhere, something is quietly getting better.

